tion": "city-holding children"}, {"id": "polites-orth1", "translation": "citizen"}, {"id": "polites-def1", "translation": "citizen"}, {"id": "polites-def2", "translation": "holding the city"}, {"id": "polites-def3", "translation": "Epic form"}, {"id": "polites-note1", "translation": "Κάδμου [of Cadmus]"}, {"id": "polites-note2", "translation": "Πολίταις τάσδε διαδρόμους [to the citizens these running through]"}, {"id": "polites-note3", "translation": "Ὡς [as]"}, {"id": "polites-note4", "translation": "Ἐπ᾿ ἀμφιβόλοισιν ἰάπτουσι πολίταις χερμάδ᾽ [upon the citizens hurling stones with both hands]"}, {"id": "polites-note5", "translation": "Ἄροισθε κύδος τοῖσδε [raise glory for these]"}, {"id": "polites-note6", "translation": "Ἢ ξὺν πολίταις ἀνδράσιν δίκαιος ὢν [or being just with citizen men]"}, {"id": "polites-note7", "translation": "where in some copies it is wrongly ξυμπολίταις [fellow-citizens]."}, {"id": "polites-note8", "translation": "Ἐρξάτην πολλὰ μὲν [they did many things]"}, {"id": "polites-note9", "translation": "Δεῖμα [fear]"}, {"id": "polites-note10", "translation": "Φίλον [dear]"}, {"id": "polites-note11", "translation": "Τὸν ἀκαίρως πόλιν οἰκουροῦντα [the one untimely guarding the city]"}, {"id": "polites-note12", "translation": "Ἄνδρες [men]"}, {"id": "polites-note13", "translation": "Πολίταις πάντ᾽ [to the citizens all]"}, {"id": "polites-note14", "translation": "Πειράσομαι ἄρχειν [I will try to rule]"}, {"id": "polites-note15", "translation": "Πολίτας [citizens]"}, {"id": "polites-note16", "translation": "Ἄνευ [without]"}, {"id": "polites-note17", "translation": "[When their own citizens do not embitter the laws.]"}, {"id": "polites-note18", "translation": "Γελῶμαι [I am laughed at]"}, {"id": "polites-note19", "translation": "Τιμιώτερος χρόνος ἔσται [Time will be more honored]"}, {"id": "polites-note20", "translation": "Τοῖσδε [to these]"}, {"id": "polites-note21", "translation": "Μέλαν αἷμα [black blood]"}, {"id": "polites-note22", "translation": "Εἴη